Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e52f51ee-9c79-6d49-b797-e891c847d157"],

Cell["\<\
Many advanced NMR and spin-based quantum experiments neither fit a single \
terminal operator transfer nor permit rigid unitary phase matrices. Examples \
include synthesising multi-axis rotations cooperatively across one pulse (or \
even different spin systems simultaneously), steering spin order around \
rapidly relaxing forbidden intermediate eigenstates, compressing gate \
durations via virtual-Z post-pulse frame rotations, isolating computational \
subspaces with bounded leakage, and jointly optimising variable inter-pulse \
delays.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b832f6c0-db11-b64b-a97d-ea639c552881"],

Cell["\<\
Synthesise multi-transformation pulses with CooperativeObjective and \
heterogeneous OptimalControlEnsemble.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"030e7141-4789-104d-8f26-f85ab0cb1a81"],

Cell["\<\
Suppress transient intermediate-state populations using RunningCost -> \
StatePenalty.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bbb540ab-9a8f-3b46-a693-d5b675ad8a4f"],

Cell["\<\
Optimise embedded gates and virtual-Z frames with SubspaceUnitaryTarget, \
LeakageWeight, and PhaseFreedom.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1e845dd7-0cee-dd49-87f1-8e354f9a9fef"],

Cell["\<\
Refine slice durations and echo delays analytically using OptimizeDurations \
and FixedTotalDuration.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7f51bd4c-715b-2c4e-afd8-90dedff11f6c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Mathematical Background", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6bf6ff66-4363-3947-b075-bb3da857f9e0"],

Cell["\<\
CooperativeObjective[{spec_1, ..., spec_R}] optimises Phi_coop = Sum_r w_r \
Phi_r (with NormalizeWeights -> True by default). RunningCost adds sum_j s_j \
phi_run(F_j, t_j, j) across coarse slice endpoints and injects boundary \
cotangents directly into the backward GRAPE sweep.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"188e71d1-ffa3-6442-9f93-434180e7a3c6"],

Cell["\<\
For embedded k-dimensional isometries V (V^dag V = I_k, W = V^dag U_T V), \
SubspaceUnitaryTarget optimises Phi_sub(W) - LeakageWeight * L(U_T), where \
L(U_T) = 1 - Tr[W^dag W]/k. Parametric virtual-Z PhaseFreedom wraps U_eff = \
P_L^dag(phi_L) U_T P_R^dag(phi_R) with analytical phase derivatives optimised \
jointly alongside RF amplitudes and slice durations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e274989-f478-df4b-8cf0-283d42f70701"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Worked Example", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a0046716-e06f-d044-a0a5-0a4f4f2454d5"],

Cell["\<\
Reproduce validated calculations from Tutorials 05 and 10: weighted \
cooperative universal pi_x, heterogeneous N=1+N=2 co-design, RunningCost \
suppression of |alpha,beta>, SubspaceUnitaryTarget Hadamard on {2,3}, \
parametric BothZ CNOT, and DelaysOnly echo delay tuning.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fff5de26-d423-da4d-b2cf-b0f4c075bbb6"],

